   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the mental hygiene law, in relation to the autism detection\nand education program and mapping of autism locations; and to amend a chapter\nof the laws of 2021 amending the mental hygiene law relating to the autism\ndetection and education program and mapping of autism locations, as proposed\nin legislative bills numbers S. 2911 and A. 1953, in relation to the\neffectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7815",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7815-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §13.42, Ment Hyg L; amd §2, Chap of 2021 (as proposed in S.2911 & A.1953)",
    "lawSection": "Mental Hygiene Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7815\n\nSPONSOR: PARKER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the mental hygiene law, in relation to the autism\ndetection and education program and mapping of autism locations; and to\namend a chapter of the laws of 2021 amending the mental hygiene law\nrelating to the autism detection and education program and mapping of\nautism locations, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 2911 and\nA. 1953, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.\n2021, c.804, by directing the Autism Spectrum Disorders Advisory Board\nto discuss autism mapping in New York State and to report on a State\nUniversity of New York study, entitled \"Exploratory spatial analysis of\nautism rates in New York school districts.\"\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by directing the Autism\nSpectrum Disorders Advisory Board to discuss screening and detection,\npromotion of education, promotion of counseling and referral services,\nand a 2020 State University of New York study published in the Journal\nof Neurodevelopmental Disorders, entitled \"Exploratory spatial analysis\nof autism rates in New York school districts\" instead of establishing an\nautism detection, education and mapping program within the board as\nproposed in the original bill.  Additionally, the board is directed to\ninclude information related to screening and detection, promotion of\neducation, promotion of counseling and referral services, and the State\nUniversity of New York study, \"Exploratory spatial analysis of autism\nrates in New York school districts\" in its annual report. The legis-\nlation also adds a sunset date on December 31, 2022.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nMental Hygiene Law § 13.42\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPursuant to approval memo 154 of 2021, this legislation is a negotiated\nchange to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 804 of the Laws of 2021. S.2911 and A.1953\nboth passed the Senate and Assembly, respectfully, in June 2021.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2021 amending the mental hygiene law relating to\nthe autism detection and education program and mapping of autism\nlocations, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.2911 and A.1953,\ntakes effect.\n",
